The pinned upstream source is carried with one local patch:
  patches/0001-guard-dimensions-and-allocations.patch

This patch records exactly the changes to src/screen.c and src/vterm.c made
by kilix-multiplexer commit 13dad84d7cf5093c9ac690da3c40c3b038b2197a. It adds
signed cell-index and allocation-size guards, plus allocation failure checks.
No additional upstream source changes are part of this patch series.

SHA256SUMS retains the original upstream file hashes. `make check-vendor`
copies the manifest files to a private temporary tree, reverses patches/series
in reverse order with zero fuzz, and verifies every restored file against
those original hashes. It also rejects unlisted source files or patches.
The check never edits this vendored tree and needs Python 3 and `patch`.

For future modifications, add a numbered patch to patches/ and list it in
patches/series. Preserve original upstream hashes; do not bless patched files
by rehashing the manifest. Upstream already surfaces Kitty graphics APC
sequences through vterm_screen_set_unrecognised_fallbacks() in wire order, so
no graphics-specific patch is needed.
